# Cookbook tutorial standards

When editing cookbook notebooks, sample markdown, or README recipe entries, follow the **cookbook-tutorial-voice** skill (`.cursor/skills/cookbook-tutorial-voice/SKILL.md`).

Align terminology and tone with Istari Digital documentation: `../istari-documentation/.cursor/rules/documentation-standards.mdc`.

**Quick rules:**

- Tutorials: numbered "You will" outcomes, concise section intros, pause callouts for web app checks
- **Istari Digital** / **Istari Digital web app** / **Istari Digital Platform** — use precisely
- Prerequisites must show the correct `uv sync --group dev` (and `--group advanced` for workflow-logs)
- Link to `docs.istaridigital.com` for concepts covered in official guides
- Split large walkthroughs into focused notebooks rather than one long demo
